  "note": "One pinch-in over the piano roll as a dual-delivery WKWebView build sends it: a ctrl-wheel AND WebKit's gesturestart/gesturechange/gestureend for the same fingers, interleaved. Written from WebKit's GestureEvent contract — cumulative `scale` starting at 1 on gesturestart, monotone through the pinch, gestureend on lift — because no machine in this repo's CI can produce one: Chromium has never implemented GestureEvent. TO REPLACE THIS WITH A REAL TRACE: build webcore's dist, point the shell at it with the disk-bundle override (shell/Source/bridge/WebResources.cpp), load the plugin in a host, paste the RECORDER snippet from scripts/scrollzoom-probe.mjs into the webview, pinch the trackpad, and paste window.__RSGT__.events in here with provenance set to 'captured'. Nothing else changes: scripts/gesture-test.ts reads the provenance field and asserts accordingly. Until somebody does that, every claim in this repo about WKWebView TIMING is a claim about the shape, and the claim about our HANDLERS — one gesture, one zoom command — is proven live in scripts/scrollzoom-probe.mjs, which dispatches this same shape at the real app.",
